WebGPU: read-write images only with texture-formats-tier2

BGFX_CAPS_IMAGE_RW was always set. Core WebGPU allows read-write storage textures in r32float, r32uint and
r32sint only, and texture-formats-tier2 adds a list of formats; an application that checked the cap bound
read-write images WebGPU refused. Formats outside tier2's list, such as rg11b10ufloat, stay read-only or
write-only: the cap has no per-format form.

diff --git a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
--- a/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer_webgpu.cpp
@@ -1510,7 +1510,7 @@ WGPU_IMPORT
 							| BGFX_CAPS_BLEND_INDEPENDENT
 							| BGFX_CAPS_COMPUTE
 							| BGFX_CAPS_DRAW_INDIRECT
-							| BGFX_CAPS_IMAGE_RW
+							| (isFeatureSupported(WGPUFeatureName_TextureFormatsTier2) ? BGFX_CAPS_IMAGE_RW : 0)
 							| BGFX_CAPS_INDEX32
 							| BGFX_CAPS_PRIMITIVE_ID
 							| BGFX_CAPS_RENDERER_MULTITHREADED
